{title: 653 - Lead Them, My God, to Thee}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Home}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]Lead them, my [Bb]God, to [Gm/Bb]Thee,
[Gm]Lead them [C]to Thee,
[C7]These children [F]dear of mine,
[F/A]Thou [Bb]gavest [Gm/Bb]me;
[Gm]O, by [C]Thy [C7]love divine,
[C]Lead them, my [F/C]God, [C7/E]to [Bb/F]Thee;
[F]Lead them, my God, to Thee,
[C7/G]Lead [F]them to [C]Thee.

Verse 2:
[F]When earth looks bright and [Bb]fair, Festive [Gm/Bb]and [Am]gay,
[C7]Let no [F]delusive snare Lure them astray;
[C]But from temptation's power, [F/C]Lead [C7/E]them, my God, [Bb/F]to Thee,
[C7/G]Lead them, [F]my God, to Thee, [C]Lead them to Thee.

Verse 3:
[F]E'en for such little [Bb]ones, Christ [Gm/Bb]came a [Am]child,
[C7]And in [F]this world of sin Lived undefiled.
[C]O, for His sake, I [F/C]pray, Lead them, [C7/E]my God, [Bb/F]to Thee,
[C7/G]Lead them, [F]my God, to Thee, [C]Lead them to Thee.

Verse 4:
[F]Yea, though my faith be [Bb]dim, I would [Gm/Bb]believe
[C7]That Thou [F]this precious gift Wilt now receive;
[C]O take their young hearts [F/C]now, Lead them [C7/E]my God [Bb/F]to Thee,
[C7/G]Lead them, [F]my God, to Thee, [C]Lead them to Thee.
